      "math_academy_id": "q-43908",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product.",
      "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3\\cdot 3+4\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (-2))+7\\cdot (0\\cdot 0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
